# Step-by-Step to Push Code to GitHub (Very Simple)

Assume your file name is:

```text id="4m6r8v"
index.html
```

---

# STEP 1 — Create GitHub Account

Go to:

[GitHub Signup](https://github.com/signup?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

Create account and login.

---

# STEP 2 — Install Git

Download Git:

[Download Git](https://git-scm.com/downloads?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

Install normally:

* Next
* Next
* Install

---

# STEP 3 — Open VS Code

Open folder containing:

```text id="oaqx1g"
index.html
```

---

# STEP 4 — Open Terminal in VS Code

Menu:

```text id="nshn0w"
Terminal → New Terminal
```

---

# STEP 5 — Initialize Git

Run:

```bash id="1v7u9j"
git init
```

---

# STEP 6 — Add Files

Run:

```bash id="wmp27r"
git add .
```

---

# STEP 7 — Commit Files

Run:

```bash id="sx1vul"
git commit -m "Responsive website project"
```

---

# STEP 8 — Create Repository on GitHub

Go to:

[GitHub](https://github.com?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

Click:

```text id="v0qqtt"
New Repository
```

Repository Name:

```text id="72r4lr"
responsive-website
```

Click:

```text id="2htl17"
Create Repository
```

---

# STEP 9 — Connect Local Project to GitHub

Copy repository URL.

Example:

```bash id="dz1w7z"
https://github.com/yourname/responsive-website.git
```

Run:

```bash id="yhnw91"
git remote add origin https://github.com/yourname/responsive-website.git
```

---

# STEP 10 — Push Code to GitHub

Run:

```bash id="ifx77z"
git branch -M main
```

Then:

```bash id="4bdb83"
git push -u origin main
```

---

# IF ASKING USERNAME/PASSWORD

GitHub now uses:

* Personal Access Token (PAT)

NOT normal password.

---

# STEP 11 — Generate GitHub Token

Go to:

[GitHub Tokens](https://github.com/settings/tokens?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

Steps:

1. Generate new token
2. Select:

   * repo
3. Generate token
4. Copy token

Use:

* Username = GitHub username
* Password = token

---

# SUCCESS

Your code is uploaded to GitHub ✅

Repository link example:

```text id="29r55p"
https://github.com/yourname/responsive-website
```

---

# COMMANDS ONLY (IMPORTANT FOR PRACTICAL)

```bash id="g24py3"
git init
git add .
git commit -m "Responsive website project"
git branch -M main
git remote add origin https://github.com/yourname/responsive-website.git
git push -u origin main
```

